{
  "requirement": "The SDK presents node inputs using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\nIts text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet contents = domain.node_content(&node_id)?;\nlet text = contents.format();\n```\n\nLoading and fallible preparation occur in `Domain::node_content` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`. For inputs queued on an ask\nbuilder, these failures return `ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node`\ntool call, they are returned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue\nand recover.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The marked tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.\n\n**1. Inputs are presented with `NodeContents::format`.**\n- Queued ask-builder inputs: `src/agent/tests.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` sets a custom formatter that outputs `formatted input: …`. It asserts the first user message contains `formatted input: source`, so the SDK uses the formatted value rather than the raw content.\n- Order and repetition: `src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` checks that the contents passed to the agent keep order and repetition.\n- `read_node` tool path: `fn[agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` uses `distinct_pages`. Its `ParallelConversations` provider asserts that the delivered `read_node` and `get_next_page` results contain the formatter-only `ALPHA-CONTENTS` or `BETA-CONTENTS` text. The tool path therefore presents the formatted text. The test also checks that `read_node` result bytes are positive. The same assertions run in the unmarked `concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads`.\n- Domain-level formatting: `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` and `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]` check the real domain's formatted text and the order of the contents in the message.\n\n**2. Text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` reads a snapshot, then changes the underlying content. It asserts `format()` still returns `before`, the fingerprint equals the snapshot fingerprint (`before`), and there was exactly one read.\n- The ask test above records the dependency fingerprint `source` and a single read for the same text.\n\n**3. Failure behavior.**\n- Queued inputs: `fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]` asserts `ValidationError::Graph(\"read\")` for a loading failure and `ValidationError::Graph(\"render\")` for a preparation failure. It also asserts that no agent request is made and that no dependency is recorded on the preparation failure.\n- `read_node` tool call: `fn[node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents]` makes `node_content` fail. It asserts the next request carries an error tool result (`is_error`, name `read_node`, the error text). The conversation then continues to `submit_result` and succeeds, and no dependency is recorded.\n\nThe loading and preparation errors share the same `Domain::node_content` error path, so the single tool-error scenario is representative. The test `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` adds no coverage for this requirement.\n\nThe obligation that formatting needs no further reads belongs to the cited `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`, which is not reassessed here. The `format()` assertions after the content changes also show the retained value is used.\n\nI found no uncovered obligation, no wrong expected result, and no marking gap.",
  "references": "2f91eb887272d526f4a252d54e6afbef9806450ccce1db796d72de96bb1e8334",
